    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nCython crashes with an unhandled KeyError instead of a normal compile error when a fused type is wrapped in a `const` qualifier and/or a pointer, in\nthree different code patterns:\n\n1. A `const <fused>[:]` local variable, unrelated to any fused-typed\n   parameter of the enclosing function.\n2. A pointer-to-`const <fused>` argument passed to a separately-declared\n   (cimported) fused cdef function.\n3. A `const <fused>` argument on a method inside a `cdef class`.\n\nAll three fail at the same point: `PyrexTypes.py`, in\n`get_all_specialized_function_types`, on the line:\n\n```\n    fused_to_specific[arg.type] if arg.is_fused else arg\n```\n\n`fused_to_specific` only contains an entry for the bare fused type, not for the composite type wrapping it (`CQualifierType(const, FusedType)` or\n`CPtrType(CQualifierType(const, FusedType))`), so the dict lookup raises KeyError.\n\nThis appears likely to be a regression from #7656 (\"new export/import naming scheme for fused C functions\"), which landed between 3.3.0a1 and\n3.3.0a2 per the CHANGES.rst entry for 3.3.0a2. Possibly also related to #7778 (cpdef fused functions generated redundant code). \nCython 3.3.0a1 does not reproduce this crash on the same code; 3.3.0a2.dev0 does.\n\n<img width=\"695\" height=\"137\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fc8e8881-b63c-46de-b4b9-5718e567a157\" />\n\n\n[These were found in scikit-learn's CI](scikit-learn/scikit-learn#34344). \n[Here is the link for the unit tests failing](https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/actions/runs/29178689752/job/86612508884)\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\nConfirmed on Cython master (installed via `pip install \"cython @ git+https://github.com/cython/cython.git@master\"`, reports version 3.3.0a2.dev0). Does not reproduce on Cython 3.3.0a1.\n\nrepro_blas.pxd:\n\n```\n    from cython cimport floating\n    cdef void _copy(int, const floating*, int, const floating*, int) noexcept nogil\n```\n\nrepro_blas.pyx:\n\n```\n    from cython cimport floating\n    cdef void _copy(int n, const floating *x, int incx, const floating *y, int incy) noexcept nogil:\n        pass\n```\n\nrepro.pyx:\n\n```\n    from cython cimport floating\n    from repro_blas cimport _copy\n\n    def f(floating[:, :] L):\n        cdef floating *L1\n        L1 = &L[0, 0]\n        _copy(1, L1, 1, L1, 1)\n``` \n\n<img width=\"961\" height=\"490\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/13146e6e-2290-46e2-b884-32ca63b01fef\" />\n<img width=\"1007\" height=\"787\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/10ce7c2d-542e-4236-a28d-3b083b13efdd\" />\n<img width=\"1262\" height=\"605\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3e4f7490-197d-440e-944d-34dd0c6dbea8\" />\n\nRun: cython repro_blas.pyx && cython repro.pyx\n\nCrashes with:\n    KeyError: <CPtrType <CQualifierType const FusedType(name='floating')>>\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nCython should either compile this code successfully (if the const/pointer composite over a fused type is meant to be supported), or output a normal,\nreadable compile-time error explaining the unsupported construct, not crash internally with an unhandled KeyError and a raw Python traceback.\n\n### OS\n\nWindows (via WSL2, Ubuntu); also affects native Linux (scikit-learn CI)\n\n### Python version\n\n3.12.3 (local repro); 3.14 (original scikit-learn CI crash)\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0a2.dev0 (crashes)\n\n### Additional context\n\nReproduces independently of target Python version (confirmed on 3.12.3 and 3.14), indicating this is a Cython compiler-internal bug rather than a\nPython 3.14 compatibility issue. Confirmed still present on Cython master as of 2026-07-12.\n\n\nAdditional:\nFull tracebacks from scikit-learn's CI, show three independent crash sites hitting the same line in PyrexTypes.py:\nError compiling Cython file:\n\n  ------------------------------------------------------------\n  ```\n  # The multinomial deviance loss is also known as categorical cross-entropy or\n  # multinomial log-likelihood.\n  # Here, we do not inherit from CyLossFunction as its cy_gradient method deviates\n  # from the API.\n  cdef class CyHalfMultinomialLoss():\n  ^\n  ------------------------------------------------------------\n  sklearn/_loss/_loss.pyx:2000:0: Compiler crash in ForwardDeclareTypes\n\n  Compiler crash traceback from this point on:\n    File \"/home/runner/miniconda3/envs/testvenv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/Cython/Compiler/Visitor.py\", line 174, in _visit\n      return handler_method(obj)\n    File \"/home/runner/miniconda3/envs/testvenv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/Cython/Compiler/ParseTreeTransforms.py\", line 2129, in visit_CClassDefNode\n      entry.type.get_all_specialized_function_types()\n      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\n    File \"/home/runner/miniconda3/envs/testvenv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/Cython/Compiler/PyrexTypes.py\", line 3975, in get_all_specialized_function_types\n      fused_to_specific[arg.type] if arg.is_fused else arg\n      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^\n  KeyError: <CQualifierType const FusedType(name='floating_in')>\n\n\nError compiling Cython file:\n  ------------------------------------------------------------\n  ...\n          m /= sizeof(double)\n\n      # delete row go_out\n      L1 = &L[0, 0] + (go_out * m)\n      for i in range(go_out, n-1):\n          _copy(i + 2, L1 + m, 1, L1, 1)\n               ^\n  ------------------------------------------------------------\n  /home/runner/work/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/sklearn/utils/arrayfuncs.pyx:103:13: Compiler crash in AnalyseExpressionsTransform\n\n  Compiler crash traceback from this point on:\n    File \"/home/runner/miniconda3/envs/testvenv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/Cython/Compiler/ExprNodes.py\", line 6538, in analyse_c_function_call\n      entry = overloaded_entry.best_function_match(\n          env,\n      ...<2 lines>...\n          arg_is_lvalue_array=[arg.is_lvalue() for arg in args],\n      )\n    File \"/home/runner/miniconda3/envs/testvenv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/Cython/Compiler/Symtab.py\", line 282, in best_function_match\n      functypes = self.type.get_all_specialized_function_types()\n    File \"/home/runner/miniconda3/envs/testvenv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/Cython/Compiler/PyrexTypes.py\", line 3975, in get_all_specialized_function_types\n      fused_to_specific[arg.type] if arg.is_fused else arg\n      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^\n  KeyError: <CPtrType <CQualifierType const FusedType(name='floating')>>\n\n```\n\nA third crash site (sparsefuncs_fast.pyx, KeyError on CPtrType<CQualifierType const FusedType(name='floating')>) occurs from a\n`const floating[:]` local variable declaration; \n\n[See the linked scikit-learn issue #34344 ](https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/34344)\n",
